# Lists: {number of: id} writes the number of an item with an Id, in the format of its list.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Lists · Citing an item
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Section:
		Text: Lists
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Citing an item
		Paragraph: An item with `Id` can be cited from any text with `{{number of: id}}`, which writes only its own number in the format of its list: `3`, `c` or `IV`.
			Style: intro
		Paragraph: The payment is regulated by clause {number of: payment}, and the cases of withdrawal by clauses {number of: withdrawal} and {number of: notice}.
			Style: sample
		List:
			Marker: upper-roman
			List item:
				Paragraph: The supplier delivers the furniture within six weeks.
			List item:
				Paragraph: The customer checks the furniture on delivery.
			List item:
				Paragraph: The customer may withdraw from the order:
				List:
					Marker: lower-alpha
					Marker suffix: parenthesis
					List item:
						Paragraph: before the furniture is made.
					List item:
						Id: withdrawal
						Paragraph: within 14 days of the delivery.
					List item:
						Id: notice
						Paragraph: with a written notice.
			List item:
				Id: payment
				Paragraph: Payment is made within 30 days of the invoice.
